		{"id":"7cef5093130a6630","type":"group","ratio":1.7777777777777777,"x":-500,"y":1420,"width":1483,"height":834,"label":"Practitioner Review: Definition, recognition, and treatment challenges of irritability in young people"},
		{"id":"50b396a4b5377a22","type":"group","x":-444,"y":540,"width":1372,"height":180,"color":"5","label":"Modules Related to Irritability"},
		{
			"id":"7dcfc54889b7cb55",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"### **Phasic Irritability**\n\n- Brief, intense temper outbursts or rage episodes\n    \n- Triggered by frustration, blocked goals, or perceived threat\n    \n- Disproportionate to the situation\n    \n- Followed by a return toward baseline mood\n    \n\n**For Example:** Explosive reactions when something goes wrong.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":1040,
			"width":624,
			"height":240
		},
